    {
      "cve": "CVE-2026-129113",
      "ids": [
        {
          "system_name": "SUSE CVE Page",
          "text": "https://www.suse.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-129113"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        {
          "category": "general",
          "text": "JSON::XS versions from 4.0_00 before 4.05 for Perl corrupt the incremental buffer length by chopping past its end in incr_skip after a top-level number.\n\nThe incremental parser scans any run of digits, signs, dots and exponent markers as one number, but the decoder stops at the end of a valid number, so the parser keeps an offset into bytes it has not decoded. It then empties the buffer without clearing those bytes, and a later incr_parse call without new input reads them again and moves the offset past the end of the buffer. incr_skip, the documented recovery after an error, removes that many bytes and the buffer length wraps.\n\nA peer sending input such as \"1-2\" to an incr_parse consumer can make the next read of incr_text exit the process through perl's uncatchable out-of-memory path.",
          "title": "CVE description"
        }
      ],
      "product_status": {
        "recommended": [
          "openSUSE Tumbleweed:perl-JSON-XS-0:4.50.0-1.1.aarch64",
          "openSUSE Tumbleweed:perl-JSON-XS-0:4.50.0-1.1.ppc64le",
          "openSUSE Tumbleweed:perl-JSON-XS-0:4.50.0-1.1.s390x",
          "openSUSE Tumbleweed:perl-JSON-XS-0:4.50.0-1.1.x86_64"
        ]
